A||||8||mrfixit58||Motor Mount Replacement. on a V6||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||07-12-2000||09:24 PM||||I think I've got a bad motor mount. I know my dog bone is garbage. I plane on replacing both this weekend. Are there any tricks that will make replaceing it any easier?<P>Roy||||reg||5
Z||000001||tgowens||07-12-2000||10:49 PM||||Roy, you can send that Blue '87 up to me in KY and i'll replace them both for you and return the car to you (maybe) in five, no ten, wait, make that 15 years..........<P>Seriously, see if you can get fieroshop on here to help, or email him at  <A HREF="mailto:fieroshp@pacbell.net">fieroshp@pacbell.net</A>  believe me, he knows the Fiero and has tricks up his sleeve even when he isn't wearing a shirt!<P>------------------<BR>     '87 Fiero GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tgowens.com/t_g_owens.gif">       <BR><A HREF="http://www.tgowens.com/fiero" TARGET=_blank>www.tgowens.com/fiero</A>||||reg||1
Z||000002||2birds||07-12-2000||10:57 PM||||I changed my junk front motor mount (the one behind the pulley) 4 weeks ago.  A half hour job ended up taking 2 hours because the Sealed Power mount I got at Discount Auto didn't fit.  The studs were not spaced properly, about 3/8 of an inch off, top and bottom.  After much cursing and complaining, and thoughts of just slotting the existing holes in the cradle and engine mount bracket, I drove 40 miles to Brunswick to my nearest Autozone and got their brand, which was a perfect match, and cost 2 bucks less to boot.  The hardest part is removing and re-installing the two bolts for the bracket that mounts the motor mount to the engine block.  Pulling the right rear wheel and inner fender liner helps, but not that much.  Make sure you put a big board under the oil pan, since the pan will dimple real easy.<BR>I may get crazy and replace my transaxle mounts, too, but they're still aligned okay.  New tires and a steering rack have a higher priority.<P>Have fun.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfixit58||07-13-2000||08:12 AM||||tgowens: I'll have to think about your offer. Hummm..... NO!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>2birds: Looks like I'm off to AutoZone. I'll let you know how the job turns out.<P>Thanks,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000004||Alex4mula||07-13-2000||08:47 AM||||Which year is your car? I don't know pre 88s, but with my cradle out I replaced that front mount in my Formula. One of the most exhausting items in my 3.4 swap. Those two screws are hell to take out because there is so little room. With the cradle on should be worst but not impossible. Just prepare your mind and have lots of patience. Wish you luck.||||reg||11
Z||000005||mrfixit58||07-13-2000||02:37 PM||||Alex4mula,<P>Thanks for the advice. Mine is an 87 GT, 5-speed. I was hoping that this would be a 15-20 minute job and was hoping to tackle it tonight (I can usually squeeze about an hour in the garage on weeknights). Sounds like it may be better left until I have a couple of hours???<P>Right now, I don't know that the motor mount is bad. I do know the bushings in the dog bone are GONE. If I shift to quickly I get an awful "thump" from the engine compartment so I went ahead and bought the mount. Am I on the right track by assuming the motor mount is bad?<P>Thanks,<BR>Roy<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000006||Pontiaddict||07-13-2000||05:19 PM||||Mrfixit, I have the same problem. I think that the dogbone is the cause of most of it.<BR>You are so lucky, I went to autozone today, they couldn't find the part. They kept looking for motor mounts on the computer. What's the technical name supposed to be anyway? Something like torque strut? If it was then they didn't have it in stock.<BR>How much did it cost? NAPA wanted $50 for it and still had to order it. I'll just hold off  until I can get some answers here.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Gold-86SE||07-14-2000||10:53 AM||||<BR>I suggest you replace the bushings in the dogbone (torque strut) with poly bushings from the Fiero Store, it is only $25 w/o tax, ordered today, you'll have them in short order. When I ordered mine, the mail time was two days.<P>Btw, once I replaced the torque strut bushings the thump went away in the engine compartment, but my other mounts need replacing, just haven't done it.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000008||mrfixit58||07-14-2000||02:18 PM||||Pontiaddict:  What I bought at Autozone was the motor mount, not the dog bone. I haven't had a chance to see if mine was bad but wanted it just in case. <P>Gold-86SE:  The poly dog bone bushings will be a future mod. I have an extra factory dog bone from a junk car so, at least for now, I'll use it.<P>Thanks,<BR>Roy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||2
